    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0320" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg192"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.1412Anti-War/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hawks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-07T10:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                                1928—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:10
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>109. Department’s circular of August 16, midnight. Note received from the Foreign
                        Office<anchor n="62" xml:id="d165-f1"/> states in part that the Government
                    of Guatemala “accepts in principle all the bases of the Anti-War Treaty to which
                    it will adhere opportunely in conformity with the conditions of the Pact
                    itself.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
